Project: CollegeWebsite
FIRST: On GitHub in your browser, create a NEW EMPTY repository named CollegeWebsite.
Do not add a README, license, or .gitignore on GitHub.
Copy its HTTPS URL, for example:
https://github.com/USERNAME/CollegeWebsite.git
Create the local project:
1. cd ~/Desktop
2. mkdir CollegeWebsite
3. cd CollegeWebsite
4. printf "<!doctype html>\n<html>\n<head><title>College Website</title></head>\n<body><h1>Welcome to Our College</h1></body>\n</html>\n" > index.html
5. printf "College website project\n" > README.md
Initialize, stage, and commit:
6. git init
7. git branch -M main
8. git status
9. git add .
10. git status
11. git commit -m "Initial CollegeWebsite project"
Connect the local repository to GitHub and push:
12. git remote add origin https://github.com/USERNAME/CollegeWebsite.git
13. git remote -v
14. git push -u origin main
Make a subsequent update and push it:
15. printf "\n<p>About our college</p>\n" >> index.html
16. git status
17. git add index.html
18. git commit -m "Updated college website"
19. git push
20. git log --oneline
21. git status
